+# Claude tools: City Sample preservation diagnostics
+
+Claude-owned and independent of Codex's `tools/` and `tests/`. Nothing here imports or changes
+Codex files, except that `run_patch_checks.py` *runs* Codex's suites on a temporary patched export.
+`AGENTS.md` limits Claude to `docs/claude/`. The owner's brief explicitly asked for runnable
+diagnostic tools, so code lives here in a new folder instead, and Codex can move or adopt it.
+
+| File | Runs where | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `cs_project_scan.py` | Any Python 3.9+, no Unreal | Offline: required plugins, project-local plugins, maps, integration-relevant asset *file names*, World Partition external-actor counts, Content size |
+| `cs_diag_editor.py` | Unreal Editor Python (PIE for runtime checks) | Read-only traffic/crowd/ZoneGraph/Mass/streaming evidence report |
+| `cs_diag_compare.py` | Any Python | Evaluate one report or diff baseline → after-migration (exit 1 on FAIL/regression) |
+| `cs_diag_core.py` | Library | Classification and checks. Missing evidence is UNKNOWN, never PASS |
+| `cr_perf_presets.py` | Any Python / Editor Python | Runtime-only low/medium/high console-variable presets and profiling commands |
+| `run_patch_checks.py` | Linux/macOS/Windows with git and a C++ compiler | Applies `docs/claude/patches/*.patch` to a clean export and re-runs all offline checks |
+| `manifests/city_sample_expectations.json` | Data | Heuristic keywords, required plugins and thresholds. Refine locally |
+
+Offline tests:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m unittest discover -s claude_tools/tests -v
+python3 claude_tools/run_patch_checks.py
+```
+
+The tests drive the Editor script with `tests/fake_unreal.py`, which is a simulation and not Unreal.
+Usage, the migration gate and limits are in `docs/claude/CITY_SAMPLE_INTEGRATION_REVIEW.md`.
